diff --git a/docs/bring-up/j72-firmware.md b/docs/bring-up/j72-firmware.md
index 6542aaa..a5458dd 100644
--- a/docs/bring-up/j72-firmware.md
+++ b/docs/bring-up/j72-firmware.md
@@ -37,6 +37,62 @@ A native touch output must not be added until J72 firmware conversion and its
 native driver are qualified together on hardware. Successful extraction alone
 does not qualify a boot packet or the per-device calibration sequence.
 
-The existing Gen1 converter targets a different board's firmware protocol.
-Its presence is not evidence that it can convert J72's N1 personality. No
-native J72 touch firmware format or device calibration output is claimed here.
+## Native N1 candidate contract
+
+The separate `z2fw-from-z2-packet@2` step preserves the existing Z2FW version-1
+framing. It is an offline candidate; the active J72 recipe still has no
+outputs. The intended firmware name is `apple/j72-fwstart.z2fw`, with these
+parameters:
+
+```json
+{
+  "step": "z2fw-from-z2-packet@2",
+  "input": "J72.mtprops",
+  "profile": "C1F15,1",
+  "calibration_address": 268472320,
+  "calibration_size": 1024,
+  "prox_address": 268473856,
+  "prox_size": 128
+}
+```
+
+The four records, in order, are:
+
+| Record | Content |
+|---|---|
+| CONFIG (4) | Eleven little-endian u32 words: `0x818`, nine zeros, `0x103`; mode 0 and explicit legacy full-word HBPP counts |
+| SEND (1) | A 144-byte legacy blob loading 128 zero proximity bytes at `0x10009600` |
+| CALIBRATION (6) | Three little-endian u32 words: address `0x10009000`, maximum 1024 bytes, provider 0 |
+| SEND (1) | The unchanged 57,016-byte `Constructed Firmware` packet from `C1F15,1` |
+
+The generated candidate is 57,256 bytes, SHA-256
+`73ca290607695ca841867a2bf76cab4bc2f5c33b9ab5ac171de5b5580a7c0c09`.
+The proximity and firmware wire packets match the private working RAM worker
+byte for byte. An independent reconstruction of the dynamic 1008-byte and
+16-byte calibration chunks also matches that worker. These are offline
+comparisons; they do not establish that the native driver boots or handles
+touch on J72.
+
+The native N1 driver owns warm-up, reset, HBPP readiness, register calibration,
+the 65 ms calibration wait, execute and runtime discovery. Those commands must
+not also appear in this firmware file. In particular, `z2fw-from-mtprops@3`
+includes a different driver's INIT and register sequence and is not suitable
+for this native N1 loader.
+
+## Per-device calibration
+
+The firmware output contains no owner's calibration. Provider 0 consumes
+`apple,z2-cal-blob` on the touchscreen node. Existing m1n1 code copies the
+running unit's ADT `multi-touch-calibration` into that property through the
+`touchscreen0` FDT alias. Unresolved `syscfg/` references are not copied.
+
+The native driver must require exactly 1024 bytes, reject absent, all-zero and
+all-`0xff` data before powering the controller, then send it in 1008-byte and
+16-byte chunks. It must not substitute another unit's calibration or an IPSW
+default. The zero proximity packet is a separate, observed model initialization;
+it does not replace this mandatory unit calibration.
+
+Before qualifying an output, test the exact native kernel, providers, device
+tree, m1n1 and privately generated firmware together. Check the calibration
+property's presence and size without publishing its bytes, then verify boot,
+touch events, coordinates, release handling and normal cleanup on the device.
